part.text:
The endpoint returns {"status":200}. I need to write client.js that fetches it and writes to results/status.json. What format should results/status.json be? "把本地 /status 端点的 status=200 写入 results/status.json" - write the status=200 into results/status.json. Likely {"status":200}. Could also be just the raw body. The README says endpoint status=200. I think writing the response body to results/status.json makes most sense. Possibly the file should contain {"status":200}. Let me implement client.js: fetch, parse, write JSON.

Let me write it. Use Node 22 built-in fetch. Create results dir. Write the body. I'll write JSON.stringify with the status value. To be safe, write the parsed body as JSON. Since body is {"status":200}, writing body yields {"status":200}.

client.js:
```js
const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');

const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:64839/status';

async function main() {
  const res = await fetch(url);
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Request failed: ${res.status}`);
  const data = await res.json();
  const outDir = path.join(__dirname, 'results');
  fs.mkdirSync(outDir, { recursive: true });
  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(outDir, 'status.json'), JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + '\n');
  console.log('status:', data.status);
}

main().catch((err) => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });
```

Should the endpoint URL be read from README or hardcoded? README gives it. I'll hardcode. Maybe better to keep simple.

Let me write and run.

